# Web3Forms — the site is a static export, so the contact form posts to
# Web3Forms directly from the browser. The access key must carry the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix to reach the client; it is public by design (it only routes
# mail to the owner's inbox). Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in.
#
#   ACCESS_KEY   https://web3forms.com → create a form for the recipient email.
#                Then, in that form's settings, enable hCaptcha. The free plan
#                uses Web3Forms' shared hCaptcha key; no extra key is needed here.

NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
